<title>USA: Physiometrix seeks device's FDA approval.</title>
<headline>Physiometrix seeks device's FDA approval.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH BILLERICA, Mass. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Physiometrix Inc said on Monday that it filed a 510(k) application with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for its Patient State Analyzer.</p>
<p>Under this filing, the company said it is seeking marketing approval for the neuromonitoring system.</p>
<p>The Patient State Analyzer includes proprietary software which processes brain wave data and converts it to a display for anesthesiologists to evaluate a patient's brain status during surgery, Physiometrix said.</p>
</text>
